1
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,807
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,270
EUN-SU, HUI-SU AND JANG KANG

3
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,265
Who... who are you?

4
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:21,830
You need to leave now.

5
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,250
You're calling this in?

6
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,757
What'll you tell the cops?

7
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,555
That you killed your husband,

8
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,641
and he's back now?

9
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:42,185
Huh?

10
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:01,621
You're mistaking me for someone else.
Please leave.

11
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,376
Your face healed nicely.

12
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:12,297
You looked so miserable
that day at the café

13
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,591
when you broke the cup
and spilled ice all over.

14
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:16,636
You must feel so much better now.

15
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,389
Since you murdered your husband.

16
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,724
I don't know what you're talking about.

17
00:02:22,725 --> 00:02:24,978
- My husband should be home any minute.
- Who? Jin-pyo?

18
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:29,858
The last time I was here,

19
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,443
I dragged his body out.

20
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,987
Like this, right? It was a challenge.

21
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:38,282
Jin-pyo in a fucking suitcase.
His body was heavy as hell.

22
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:50,003
Your place
doesn't smell so perfumy today.

23
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:04,058
I bet that's where he put the camera.

24
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:18,031
Yep, looks like the exact angle.

25
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:27,290
Ooh. That must've hurt.

26
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,586
<i>As soon as you land, toss it.</i>

27
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:36,048
Stop. Cut it out.

28
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,550
Do you know how much it cost me
to restore this thing?

29
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:41,012
What are you doing here?

30
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,644
I like this place.

31
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,689
I'd love to see the rest of the house now.

32
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,494
Open it.

33
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:10,250
I don't know the combination.

34
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,127
Try one.

35
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:30,895
<i>The password is incorrect.</i>

36
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:40,113
<i>- The password is incorrect.</i>
- Are you serious?

37
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:43,700
Open it by tomorrow.

38
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:48,329
I'll be needing...

39
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:51,624
three billion won.

40
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,458
What?

41
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:56,129
You and Jo Eun-su murdered your husband.

42
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,756
You'll want me to keep quiet.

43
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:05,221
You've got it wrong.
Eun-su had nothing to do with it.

44
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:07,807
Three billion.

45
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:13,104
I don't have any money.

46
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:16,274
Really?

47
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,900
Then I guess I should go talk to Jin-young

48
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:20,486
down at the police station.

49
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,911
Fun times, huh?

50
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,353
It's my mother-in-law.
She's on her way here.

51
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:56,105
MOTHER

52
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:04,405
She said she's planning on
spending the night here.

53
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,789
Having a talk with her
should be interesting.

54
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,210
I thought you wanted money.

55
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:26,928
Pick up.

56
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:28,930
Tell her to piss off.

57
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,974
She'll know I'm not okay.

58
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:33,851
She'll hear it in my voice.

59
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:36,854
She might call the police.

60
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:41,734
Oh shit.

61
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,343
Wait. Someone might see you.

62
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:11,139
Now you're getting it.

63
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,734
It's fine. I'll avoid cameras.

64
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:25,653
No one will notice me.

65
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:27,822
You and Jo Eun-su,

66
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:30,032
you lucked out. You know that?

67
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,909
I can be sneaky.

68
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:33,828
You have five days.

69
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,248
Huh?

70
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:39,709
Right.

71
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:06,234
MOTHER

72
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:15,160
Hello, Mother.
Sorry I didn't answer. I was washing up.

73
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,787
<i>Did you have a bubble bath or something?</i>

74
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:18,663
Has Jin-pyo called yet?

75
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:20,457
<i>No, I haven't heard from him.</i>

76
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,043
All right.

77
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,352
Oh!

78
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:41,812
I haven't seen you around lately.

79
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,148
Were you away on business?

80
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:48,985
You know, your mother insisted
I call her the second I saw you.

81
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:50,779
I've been keeping an eye out.

82
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:53,073
Sir, I'm so happy to see you.

83
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:55,158
I'm glad that you've returned.

84
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,418
What do you want?

85
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:07,212
Like a smoke or some money or...

86
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:09,631
Goodness, sir! I wouldn't dream of it!

87
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:18,182
Hey, I forgot something... in the car.

88
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:20,518
Can you help me?

89
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:57,178
Sh.

90
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,689
No. Not that way.

91
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,327
Gotta be sneaky, right?

92
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,439
<i>Tell Jo Hui-su her phone is off.</i>

93
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,488
Who is this?

94
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,700
Why are you playing dumb?

95
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,535
You didn't know I was back?

96
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:44,786
Jang Kang?

97
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,288
Did you miss me?

98
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:47,707
I'm in Seoul.

99
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:50,208
- You promised never to come back to Korea.
- <i>Yeah.</i>

100
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:51,918
I forgot.

101
00:11:57,425 --> 00:12:00,176
I just paid Jo Hui-su a little visit.

102
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:02,179
Are you insane? You went to her house?

103
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:06,934
Three billion won. Five days.

104
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,019
Clock's ticking.

105
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:21,489
{\an8}HUI-SU

106
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:23,616
<i>The customer you are calling
is currently unavailable.</i>

107
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:25,577
<i>Please leave a message after the tone.</i>

108
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:38,256
- Whoa. Sorry. I can't let you through.
- No, wait. Just one second.

109
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:39,841
This is a crime scene. It's off limits.

110
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,551
- Settle down, ma'am.
- No, give me a second!

111
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:43,887
- I told you, you can't pass through.
- Was a woman hurt?

112
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,346
Calm down. Victim's a man.

113
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:47,850
It's the security guard.
Poor guy was found dead.

114
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:03,824
HUI-SU

115
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:07,203
<i>The customer you are calling
is currently unavailable.</i>

116
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,313
Morning, Mr. Jin.

117
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:38,900
Hui-su's late? That's not like her?

118
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:41,070
She's taken a load
off your shoulders lately, huh?

119
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,165
- Hi, what's up?
- <i>Yes, hello. Mr. Jin?</i>

120
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,543
- Has Hui-su come in today?
<i>- Not yet.</i>

121
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:58,212
She's running late.

122
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:03,050
Okay, and would you happen to know
where Mr. Jang Kang is staying?

123
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:07,470
Jang Kang?

124
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:08,930
<i>Yeah, but never mind.</i>

125
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:12,559
Could you please tell Hui-su
to give me a call when she gets to work?

126
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,977
<i>Thanks so much.</i>

127
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,231
What was that?

128
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:25,739
Morning, Mr. Jin.

129
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:30,035
Hey, uh...

130
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:32,538
Did you hear Jang Kang's back?

131
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:35,082
Oh? How'd you know?

132
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:38,043
I heard he got back two days ago,
but I haven't seen him yet.

133
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,443
Sorry, do you have a phone charger?

134
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,528
Yeah. Sure. I'll plug it in.

135
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,874
Oh, uh, it's ringing.
Could I get it back, please?

136
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,543
Of course, no problem.

137
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,265
Hello?

138
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:38,938
I opened the safe.

139
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:42,983
Yes.

140
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,701
Mom. Hi.

141
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,080
What's the matter?

142
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:57,997
What is it?

143
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:58,916
Come here.

144
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,126
I can't be away too long.

145
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:05,881
The security guard
at Jin-pyo's place died.

146
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:07,424
So what?

147
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:10,009
Look into it.

148
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,135
Ugh, I'm busy.

149
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:12,221
It's just...

150
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:18,811
I'd actually asked
that very guard to keep an eye on Hui-su.

151
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:21,145
Ugh, Ma!

152
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:23,356
She seems really off to me.

153
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:25,317
Why would you say that?

154
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,987
- Jin-pyo's the one being weird.
- Hey!

155
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:30,906
How dare you compare the two!

156
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:36,077
You don't find it strange that she hasn't
worked in forever and suddenly got a job?

157
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:38,162
She's been acting like
she doesn't mind he's gone.

158
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:40,791
Oh, Mom, why are you being like this?

159
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:46,755
Hui-su!

160
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:49,507
Where were you? Your phone wasn't on.

161
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:50,425
Oh.

162
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:53,428
- <i>Stand clear of closing doors.</i>
- I forgot to plug it in.

163
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:56,807
God, you should've called last night.
I would've rushed over here.

164
00:16:57,641 --> 00:16:59,101
You've done so much.

165
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:01,562
You're okay though, right?

166
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:03,605
Mm-hmm.

167
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:05,691
Thank God.

168
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:13,532
This won't be enough for Jang Kang.

169
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,534
So what are you gonna do?

170
00:17:16,577 --> 00:17:19,162
I'll put my mom's house up
for urgent sale.

171
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,872
I'll put this place up too.

172
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:24,043
I'll get as much money as possible
to get him to leave.

173
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:26,462
What if he comes back?

174
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:30,299
What if, after everything you give him,
he comes back to threaten you again?

175
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,886
- I'm gonna meet him and settle this.
- No, please don't.

176
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:37,805
- How can he ask for three billion won?
- Just stay out of it.

177
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:45,522
What, Hui-su?

178
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,275
Jang Kang.

179
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,613
He is way more terrifying
than you imagine.

180
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,119
He's the one who

181
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,790
killed that security guard.

182
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,128
The detectives
who came by this morning

183
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:11,673
already went through
all of Mr. Kim's stuff.

184
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:15,635
I found something else.
Just now, it was in here.

185
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:17,096
Pretty sure it was his.

186
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:18,721
Oh, okay.

187
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:19,723
Right.

188
00:18:23,894 --> 00:18:25,771
- Hello, sir.
- Yes?

189
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,147
I live in unit 703.

190
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:31,359
I was wondering about
the pest control scheduled for next week.

191
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,819
Which block are you starting with?

192
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,404
Is there any way my place
could be done before 9:00 a.m.?

193
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:38,741
Oh, I'm so sorry, ma'am.
We hired a private company to do it,

194
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:42,370
and it's against building policy
for them to start before 9:00.

195
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:54,258
Oh? Jin-young.

196
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:56,759
I get it.

197
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:59,512
I wouldn't have called 119
about the guard either.

198
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,933
We need to focus on Jang Kang for now.

199
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:04,600
He can try to blackmail you.

200
00:19:04,601 --> 00:19:06,895
But the truth is,
he has no evidence at all.

201
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:10,523
There's no way Jin-pyo's phone
will provide his whereabouts. Don't worry.

202
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,112
He can't risk meeting
with Jin-pyo's sister.

203
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:18,240
The minute he shows his face,
he'll have to give up on the money.

204
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,201
He can't come back here either.

205
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:27,416
What happened to the guard
was really tragic. I know.

206
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:31,378
But pretty soon, Jang Kang is gonna have
no other choice but to lay low.

207
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:34,714
But Eun-su, I--

208
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:35,716
No, <i>we.</i>

209
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:42,264
Mm-hmm.

210
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:49,353
This is my first case since
I transferred to the Violent Crimes Unit.

211
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:51,439
What a surprise
running into you like this.

212
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,566
I know, right?

213
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:55,902
I was at my brother's and figured
I should come see about the incident.

214
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:59,823
Well, um, I'm finding it really strange
the cameras didn't get any images.

215
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:02,283
Uh, I know the video quality
is never great,

216
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:04,536
but the drizzle last night
only made it worse.

217
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,042
Here.

218
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,085
You missed this.

219
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,879
What? Oh man!

220
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,839
Where'd you get this? Thanks so much.

221
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:18,925
Damn. How did I overlook something
so important?

222
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:22,596
Yes, hello?

223
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:25,139
- I gotta take this, okay?
- Mm.

224
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,850
Yes, I'm looking into it now.

225
00:20:59,007 --> 00:21:00,132
DELETING FILE

226
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:01,300
FILE DELETED

227
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,222
Jin-young.

228
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:06,932
Hmm?

229
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,685
- There isn't much to see, huh?
- Hmm.

230
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,352
Yeah.

231
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,562
The way I see it,

232
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:15,607
the bastard knows
how to dodge the cameras.

233
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:17,651
Or the bitch.

234
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:19,778
What?

235
00:21:22,572 --> 00:21:23,407
Huh?

236
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:26,367
Oh! You're right!

237
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:28,619
Yeah, totally.
Man, you really are the best.

238
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,122
Hey, do you have a minute?

239
00:21:31,164 --> 00:21:33,124
Remember what I asked for last time?

240
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:35,251
Have any alerts come in on that name?

241
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:43,552
Nothing yet?

242
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:46,555
So he isn't back in Korea?

243
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:52,144
Got it. Let's catch up soon.

244
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:53,603
Later.

245
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,399
Don't come back yet.

246
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:01,611
Not until I get that promotion.

247
00:22:04,489 --> 00:22:07,033
<i>The customer you are calling
is currently unavailable.</i>

248
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:08,576
<i>Please leave a message after...</i>

249
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,582
Don't you dare go near Hui-su's place.

250
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:15,459
Cops are everywhere.

251
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:18,128
I'll come to you. Pin your location.

252
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,388
MS. KIM MI-GYEONG

253
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:30,640
Yes, Mrs. Kim?

254
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,309
How about you try it on?

255
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:34,769
It's lovely.

256
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:54,998
Hey, listen. I'll be back in a moment.
Cover for me, please.

257
00:22:59,252 --> 00:23:01,755
Are you out of your mind?
This place is packed.

258
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:05,592
Scared people will think Jin-pyo's here?

259
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:07,803
Follow me.

260
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:10,472
Listen, honey.

261
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:15,310
You think you can give me orders?

262
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:17,187
You're a killer.

263
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:19,523
Are you nuts?

264
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:27,572
Someone's over there watching us.

265
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:32,160
If you want your money, follow me.

266
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:35,704
- Hello Eun-su.
- Hello.

267
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:38,500
Oh, hello.
Are you here to look at necklaces?

268
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:44,923
Oh, hell yeah.

269
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:47,508
- Pardon?
- He's kidding around.

270
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:48,635
This way, sir.

271
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:53,348
Excuse us.

272
00:23:55,308 --> 00:23:57,268
Take the red-eye to China tonight.

273
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,353
Nah.

274
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,605
Chill out, will ya?

275
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:04,316
I don't give a damn about Jin-pyo.
He's already dead.

276
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:06,611
What do you mean he's dead?
Can you prove it?

277
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,993
I knew you wanted to whack the guy.

278
00:24:14,077 --> 00:24:18,373
He beat her, kept her under surveillance,
and tracked her location.

279
00:24:21,042 --> 00:24:23,503
You two thought you were so smart.

280
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:29,176
Thing is, you had no clue the prick
was tracking his wife's every move.

281
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:31,136
Huh?

282
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:39,811
Just give me his phone.

283
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:42,772
No, I want the money first.

284
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:45,900
Hand it over, or I'll report you
for murdering the security guard.

285
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,568
So what if you report me?

286
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:51,614
Think I won't drag you down? Think I won't
tell them about you and your friend?

287
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:53,365
What would you get from doing that anyway?

288
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:56,286
If we get arrested, remember,
you won't get any money.

289
00:24:58,246 --> 00:24:59,206
Oh yeah.

290
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,084
I'll adjust my fee to include the phone.

291
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:04,460
3.1 billion.

292
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,967
This is how scared
you should've been all along.

293
00:25:11,968 --> 00:25:13,720
Shouldn't have underestimated me,
you know?

294
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:22,061
Ms. Eun-su.

295
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:24,064
- Yes?
- She's waiting for you.

296
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,778
KO JEONG-SUK’S BY YOUR SIDE

297
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:33,072
Oh, hello, Mrs. Ko.
It's an honor to meet you.

298
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:35,491
- Thank you, dear.
- I'm a huge fan of yours.

299
00:25:35,492 --> 00:25:36,867
- Hello.
- I've read all your books.

300
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:39,788
- I... I love them all.
- So lovely to hear. Thank you.

301
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,957
Oh, I... I just love her.

302
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:47,002
- Mrs. Ko. I'm such a fan.
- Nice to meet you. Sure.

303
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:48,546
- It's so wonderful to meet you.
- Yes.

304
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,089
May I take a picture with you?

305
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:51,298
Of course.

306
00:25:52,634 --> 00:25:53,884
You know, my friend,

307
00:25:53,885 --> 00:25:56,554
her marriage has improved so much
thanks to you.

308
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:58,389
But unfortunately,
she couldn't make it today.

309
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,516
- I see. Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

310
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:02,893
- Thank you.
- Hello, Mrs. Ko.

311
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,354
- I'm such a fan.
- Hello.

312
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,438
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

313
00:26:06,439 --> 00:26:08,441
- Yes. Thank you for coming.
- Of course.

314
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,492
<i>Mom, I'm on the run.</i>

315
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:24,415
Where are you?

316
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:27,377
<i>I'm out of money, Mom.
I need you to send me some.</i>

317
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:36,343
For the most part,

318
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:40,640
these remarks only worsen the relationship
rather than resolve the problem.

319
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,559
Why do you think that is?

320
00:26:43,059 --> 00:26:46,312
It's because we fail to understand
the other person's intention

321
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:49,064
and focus instead
on their choice of words.

322
00:26:49,065 --> 00:26:53,652
Conversation is the process
of understanding each other's intentions.

323
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:57,032
But we often start to talk
in a defensive mood.

324
00:26:59,576 --> 00:27:02,953
A married couple
is the beating heart of the family.

325
00:27:02,954 --> 00:27:06,040
If we understand
how the other expresses themselves.

326
00:27:06,041 --> 00:27:09,335
And keep that in mind during
the more challenging conversations...

327
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:11,880
<i>You need to keep me
and the money a secret.</i>

328
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,548
<i>And don't text back. I'll be in touch.</i>

329
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:16,884
...that communicate effectively
with each other

330
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:19,094
and share activities and experiences

331
00:27:19,095 --> 00:27:21,555
will have received
the world's greatest gift.

332
00:27:21,556 --> 00:27:23,891
- Hey, lady.
- Everyone, please...

333
00:27:23,892 --> 00:27:25,142
Keep this secret.

334
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:28,480
- It's our secret. Okay?
- It begins with one remark.

335
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:33,025
It is crucial to learn
how to listen, empathize with,

336
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:35,737
and understand each other's intentions.

337
00:27:37,989 --> 00:27:39,406
Um, Mr. Chairman,

338
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:41,492
do you think you can perhaps refer me

339
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,953
to a trustworthy agency
to handle something?

340
00:27:44,537 --> 00:27:47,499
It's not for me.
I'm asking for a client I care for.

341
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:52,671
Certainly.

342
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:56,424
Safe travels, sir.

343
00:28:03,973 --> 00:28:06,183
Hey, Jang Kang. You're here.

344
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:08,311
You really came back, huh?

345
00:28:10,605 --> 00:28:11,730
Mr. Wi.

346
00:28:11,731 --> 00:28:14,983
If you were gonna come back so soon,
why'd you leave at all?

347
00:28:14,984 --> 00:28:16,443
And, um, where are you staying now?

348
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:19,489
Oh, hey, hey, hey.
Come here. Taste some of this.

349
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:24,119
Here. Have a bite, yeah?
It's on me, okay? Eat up.

350
00:28:26,413 --> 00:28:30,124
Ah, don't mention it. It's been ages.
I'll give you a sundae too.

351
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:32,292
Ma'am, a sundae for my friend.

352
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:33,669
Ha. Here.

353
00:28:33,670 --> 00:28:35,171
- Eat up.
- I don't want any.

354
00:28:37,298 --> 00:28:38,800
Give me the bill, lady.

355
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:44,305
Wh... what?

356
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:47,183
Keep the change.
It'll cover whatever this guy orders.

357
00:28:50,019 --> 00:28:51,187
Hey, Wi.

358
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:54,899
- We should get a drink.
- Uh... Oh, okay.

359
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:03,657
Hey, go easy on them, huh?

360
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:05,993
- This guy's a shark.
- He's an expert.

361
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,504
Hey, those look good.

362
00:29:25,972 --> 00:29:28,849
Mr. Ma, the manager
of the private detective agency,

363
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,225
isn't here today.

364
00:29:30,226 --> 00:29:33,563
If he shows up,
tell him that if a Jo Eun-su should call,

365
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:36,524
he should assign his best guy to the job.

366
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:39,110
Jo Eun-su?

367
00:29:39,611 --> 00:29:41,321
Sir, it's your turn now.

368
00:29:57,086 --> 00:29:58,213
You're here, sir.

369
00:30:16,648 --> 00:30:19,275
That guy used to move boxes
at your warehouse, right?

370
00:30:20,443 --> 00:30:21,944
He was totally out of control,

371
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:23,863
so I left him there to drink
till he passed out.

372
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,740
I'm guessing he came into some money.

373
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:29,243
Why couldn't he just have
a few drinks and take it easy?

374
00:30:29,244 --> 00:30:32,163
I just finished redecorating the place.
This is terrible.

375
00:30:47,095 --> 00:30:49,347
- This should cover the damage.
- Thank you.

376
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:35,183
He used to save the broth
for instant noodles for later.

377
00:31:35,184 --> 00:31:38,729
Now he's handing out
50,000 won bills to escorts.

378
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:40,814
He used to call me "sir" out of respect.

379
00:31:40,815 --> 00:31:43,151
Now he buys the drinks and acts so rude.

380
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:45,402
I get it.

381
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:47,946
He's supposed to score
three billion won really soon,

382
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:50,449
so this kind of money
is like a joke to him now.

383
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:51,533
Three billion?

384
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:54,370
He mentioned
these two bitches that owe him.

385
00:31:55,496 --> 00:31:58,707
I mean, he's got two women
wrapped around his finger,

386
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:01,001
and they're gonna give him
the three billion.

387
00:32:02,295 --> 00:32:05,089
He's obviously scamming
or blackmailing them, sir.

388
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:11,763
Oh shit.

389
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:16,142
Mr. Jin.

390
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:22,731
What the fuck?

391
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:24,191
Who do you think you are?

392
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:26,319
You think you can put your hands
on my money?

393
00:32:30,698 --> 00:32:31,699
Huh?

394
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,959
You wrecked the place.
You need to pay, jackass.

395
00:32:42,710 --> 00:32:43,711
Also,

396
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:47,507
you're in some new business, huh?

397
00:32:48,508 --> 00:32:51,802
You wouldn't want the cops to come get you
for entering the country illegally.

398
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:57,976
Fuck, man.
What makes you think I got in illegally?

399
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:01,187
I have a passport. Actually, I have two.

400
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:03,189
There's mine and another guy's.

401
00:33:04,023 --> 00:33:08,236
Make this fucking asshole pay
for the damage and give me my cash now.

402
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,115
Now!

403
00:33:12,615 --> 00:33:13,533
Huh?

404
00:33:19,455 --> 00:33:20,623
Watch it.

405
00:33:27,255 --> 00:33:29,965
See you when you sober up, loser.
Let's go.

406
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:32,050
- Yes, sir.
- Where the fuck do you think you're going?

407
00:33:36,055 --> 00:33:37,515
Fucking hell.

408
00:33:38,683 --> 00:33:40,600
That's for messing
with one of my employees.

409
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:50,236
Fuck. Dammit!

410
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:51,737
Hey!

411
00:33:51,738 --> 00:33:53,031
Fuck you!

412
00:33:53,906 --> 00:33:54,741
Fuck!

413
00:34:04,834 --> 00:34:06,377
Could you step out a minute?

414
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:19,932
- <i>Yes, hello?</i>
- Hi, sir.

415
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:23,311
Sorry for not coming in. I'm still sick.

416
00:34:26,397 --> 00:34:28,983
- You in trouble or something?
- Not at all, sir. I'm fine.

417
00:34:32,987 --> 00:34:34,655
Okay, then. Mm.

418
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:37,075
Take care.

419
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:39,285
Come in when you're better. Okay?

420
00:34:47,251 --> 00:34:49,087
<i>Password is incorrect.</i>

421
00:35:18,074 --> 00:35:20,158
<i>Tell him that
if a Jo Eun-su should call,</i>

422
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:22,745
he should assign his best guy to the job.

423
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,248
Jo Eun-su?

424
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:31,963
MS. JO EUN-SU

425
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:53,276
<i>She should've
killed her husband.</i>

426
00:36:02,577 --> 00:36:05,663
What can they do
if there's no body to prove it?

427
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:10,793
<i>Make sure no one knows you did it,
or make sure no one knows he's dead.</i>

428
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:15,590
That's why Eun-su hired Jang Kang.

429
00:36:19,218 --> 00:36:20,761
Where's Hui-su's husband?

430
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:23,471
I have a passport.

431
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:26,683
<i>Actually, I have two.
There's mine and another guy's.</i>

432
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:28,561
Does your husband know
you're applying here?

433
00:36:29,854 --> 00:36:30,897
We're separated.

434
00:36:43,117 --> 00:36:46,621
No, she thought of that because of me.

435
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:52,460
Hey, Mr. Ma. Have you eaten yet?

436
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:54,754
Yeah.

437
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:58,799
Sir, could you get some intel on someone?

438
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:00,634
A location tracker?

439
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:04,263
Good news is I don't think Jang Kang
knows where Jin-pyo's body is.

440
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:08,184
We need to get that phone from him
before he figures it out.

441
00:37:09,018 --> 00:37:10,227
How though?

442
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:11,269
Give me a sec.

443
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:18,069
Hello, I called a little earlier today.

444
00:37:18,694 --> 00:37:20,196
I need to retrieve a phone.

445
00:37:22,114 --> 00:37:23,114
There are eyes everywhere.

446
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:25,367
Just tell me where you are.
I'll bring you the money.

447
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:28,370
- <i>Yeah, no. Call me later.</i>
- Are you at your old place?

448
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:30,414
Fuck me. I said call later!

449
00:37:46,305 --> 00:37:48,683
MANAGER HWANG

450
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:57,775
<i>Please start
by looking into motels in this area.</i>

451
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:17,271
{\an8}SAN 1, DAECHI-RI, HYEONBUK-MYEON,
YANGYANG-GUN, GANGWON-DO

452
00:39:26,781 --> 00:39:29,158
{\an8}LOCATION TRACKER

453
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:33,995
{\an8}CONNECTION LOST
WOULD YOU LIKE TO RECONNECT?

454
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:37,123
{\an8}NO RECORDS LOCATIONS

455
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:38,793
{\an8}OCTOBER 30

456
00:39:40,461 --> 00:39:42,588
That afternoon...

457
00:39:43,297 --> 00:39:45,591
...she went there before Jin-pyo died.

458
00:39:49,553 --> 00:39:51,430
What was she doing out there?

459
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:54,767
{\an8}

460
00:39:55,684 --> 00:39:58,521
{\an8}SAN 1, DAECHI-RI

461
00:40:00,898 --> 00:40:03,817
<i>Yeah, I found the motel,
but the man just got a cab and left.</i>

462
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:06,903
<i>Looks like he was in a hurry.
Want me to keep following him, ma'am?</i>

463
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:08,071
Please do that.

464
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:11,199
<i>He just took the Gangneung exit
at the Yangyang junction.</i>

465
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:13,536
<i>- Should I stay on his tail?</i>
- At Yangyang?

466
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:17,123
No, you can stop there.
Thank you. That'll be all for now.

467
00:40:24,004 --> 00:40:26,923
Ms. Jo's been trying to get her
hands on Jang Kang's phone.

468
00:40:26,924 --> 00:40:30,553
But out of nowhere, she asked us to stop
tailing him in the middle of the highway.

469
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:34,056
Sir, would you like me
to keep an eye on him?

470
00:40:50,489 --> 00:40:51,364
Uh-huh.

471
00:40:57,246 --> 00:40:58,914
Without Eun-su knowing.

472
00:41:28,611 --> 00:41:29,819
<i>Processing.</i>

473
00:41:29,820 --> 00:41:31,321
<i>Processing.</i>

474
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:32,615
<i>Please wait.</i>

475
00:41:33,115 --> 00:41:36,118
<i>Transaction complete.
Please take your cash.</i>

476
00:41:37,369 --> 00:41:40,748
<i>Never use an ATM if it appears
to have been tampered with.</i>

477
00:41:45,127 --> 00:41:47,045
Hey Hui-su. I have a work thing,

478
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:49,506
so I'll be out of reach
for the next few hours.

479
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:51,216
Did you get the phone back?

480
00:41:51,217 --> 00:41:52,759
<i>Not yet, but soon, I hope.</i>

481
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:55,638
<i>Hey. If Jang Kang calls you today,
don't pick up, okay?</i>

482
00:41:56,805 --> 00:42:00,142
- He's gonna call though.
- Just don't pick up. I'll handle the guy.

483
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:09,902
<i>Jo Eun-su.</i>

484
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:12,195
<i>Guess where.</i>

485
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:13,239
<i>Huh?</i>

486
00:42:14,448 --> 00:42:15,824
<i>Yeah, Yangyang.</i>

487
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:27,669
<i>Mount Manwol in Yangyang.</i>

488
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:38,596
<i>I bet Jin-pyo's here.</i>

489
00:42:38,597 --> 00:42:41,183
<i>He's here, isn't he? Huh?</i>

490
00:42:42,935 --> 00:42:43,852
Hey.

491
00:42:44,853 --> 00:42:46,730
What'd you think of the video I sent?

492
00:42:49,525 --> 00:42:51,527
Looks like a random mountain to me.

493
00:42:54,196 --> 00:42:58,284
I guess you girls worked really hard
to bury him in that random mountain. Huh?

494
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:00,494
I know what I'll do.

495
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:03,289
I'll bring a shovel and stuff
to go dig up there tomorrow.

496
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:06,207
I wonder what I'll find.

497
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:10,629
Sounds like fun.

498
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:12,881
I have the money though.

499
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:14,341
You wanna meet?

500
00:43:36,655 --> 00:43:38,531
<i>She looked like
she really needed money.</i>

501
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:40,993
<i>Seems a shame
to sell that place for so little.</i>

502
00:43:44,079 --> 00:43:47,415
ACE REAL ESTATE

503
00:43:47,416 --> 00:43:50,376
I added another lock
to my front door just in case.

504
00:43:50,377 --> 00:43:52,337
Here's the key. Go wait at my house.

505
00:43:52,338 --> 00:43:54,840
Uh... let's go together
when you get off work.

506
00:43:55,716 --> 00:43:57,843
Uh, I'm working late tonight.

507
00:43:58,385 --> 00:44:01,721
I think we've been letting our guard down.
Jang Kang might show up again.

508
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:03,599
Yeah, but I'm not sure
I should go there alone.

509
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:50,771
Are you the new replacement?

510
00:44:51,271 --> 00:44:54,066
<i>Mr. Hwang asked me
to handle your case from now on.</i>

511
00:44:54,566 --> 00:44:56,859
If you tell me Jang Kang's whereabouts,

512
00:44:56,860 --> 00:45:00,071
I'll find the guy and see
that he's back in China by tomorrow.

513
00:45:00,072 --> 00:45:03,033
I'll be standing by
at the location you specified.

514
00:45:33,439 --> 00:45:34,523
Jin-pyo?

515
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:43,657
That's not him.

516
00:45:44,658 --> 00:45:46,160
He isn't back in Korea.

517
00:45:54,668 --> 00:45:56,044
Is this a fuckin' joke?

518
00:46:02,259 --> 00:46:04,010
What the hell
am I supposed to do with this?

519
00:46:04,011 --> 00:46:06,138
She'll put the rest in that bag later.

520
00:46:11,059 --> 00:46:12,518
How much are we talkin'?

521
00:46:12,519 --> 00:46:13,811
We're gonna have to count it.

522
00:46:13,812 --> 00:46:17,524
Hui-su found it under the mattress
when she cleaned out her mom's place.

523
00:46:18,025 --> 00:46:19,401
Could be ten times that.

524
00:46:20,527 --> 00:46:23,739
No wonder she's in a loony bin,
pulling shit like that.

525
00:46:26,825 --> 00:46:28,202
How much longer?

526
00:46:28,869 --> 00:46:30,037
A while still.

527
00:46:41,173 --> 00:46:42,800
INSPECTOR CHOI GYEONG-GU

528
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:49,388
What's up, Choi?

529
00:46:49,389 --> 00:46:51,015
<i>Yeah, hi. Uh, well,</i>

530
00:46:51,016 --> 00:46:54,228
I've been reviewing the evidence
for the security guard's case.

531
00:46:57,105 --> 00:46:57,940
Huh?

532
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:02,986
Uh... good. That's great. You're killing it.

533
00:47:03,487 --> 00:47:05,363
<i>Thanks, but the thing is, uh,</i>

534
00:47:05,364 --> 00:47:06,864
the dashcam footage that we managed

535
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:09,409
to get from a car
that drove by around then...

536
00:47:10,077 --> 00:47:13,622
There's no easy way to say it,
but it captured your sister-in-law.

537
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:16,542
What?

538
00:47:18,293 --> 00:47:20,378
What are you trying to insinuate?

539
00:47:20,379 --> 00:47:23,464
Uh, no, nothing much.
I didn't mean anything by it.

540
00:47:23,465 --> 00:47:26,050
It's just that she was standing there,
and I found it a bit odd.

541
00:47:26,051 --> 00:47:28,095
<i>So I thought I'd call and check with you.</i>

542
00:47:29,555 --> 00:47:32,098
Uh, listen, I'm driving now.

543
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:33,099
<i>Okay, I see. Sorry.</i>

544
00:47:33,100 --> 00:47:34,643
I'll call you later, Jin-young.

545
00:47:35,602 --> 00:47:36,435
All right, goodbye.

546
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:44,361
Oh shit.

547
00:47:44,945 --> 00:47:46,989
I've got the interview tomorrow.

548
00:47:49,658 --> 00:47:51,868
Gotta get rid of the dashcam footage.

549
00:47:55,873 --> 00:47:57,332
MOM

550
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:01,169
- Mom, can I call you back? I'm busy--
- Your brother was here.

551
00:48:05,883 --> 00:48:07,967
<i>He has some terrible people after him.</i>

552
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:10,636
<i>He came to see me,
but he had to keep his distance.</i>

553
00:48:10,637 --> 00:48:14,473
Anyway, find your brother
and bring him home

554
00:48:14,474 --> 00:48:16,810
before his office gets to him.

555
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:20,354
<i>I've been rereading his messages
for the past two days.</i>

556
00:48:20,355 --> 00:48:21,940
<i>I'm worried sick.</i>

557
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:23,901
Messages?

558
00:48:28,363 --> 00:48:29,947
MOM, I'M ON THE RUNN

559
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:31,490
I'M OUT OF MONEE

560
00:48:31,491 --> 00:48:33,242
NOONE CAN NO ABOUT THE MONEE OR ME

561
00:48:40,375 --> 00:48:41,376
{\an8}JIN-PYO

562
00:48:42,711 --> 00:48:45,380
I'M HAVING DINNER WITH MOM TONIGHT
YOU CAN MAKE IT, RIGHT?

563
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:50,469
Jin-pyo didn't send any of these.

564
00:48:54,097 --> 00:48:56,183
Where are we?

565
00:49:01,438 --> 00:49:02,773
We almost there?

566
00:49:06,151 --> 00:49:07,069
Hey.

567
00:49:09,821 --> 00:49:11,740
How much longer till we get there?

568
00:49:20,832 --> 00:49:22,376
Where are we going?

569
00:49:26,505 --> 00:49:27,589
Huh?

570
00:49:32,636 --> 00:49:33,720
Let me out.

571
00:49:36,723 --> 00:49:38,099
Just stop the car!

572
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:39,892
- Let go!
- Fucking bitch!

573
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:41,520
Stop it!

574
00:49:42,354 --> 00:49:44,272
You fucking whore!

575
00:49:54,950 --> 00:49:56,158
You bitch!

576
00:49:56,159 --> 00:49:59,453
I told you to pull over.
You almost got us both killed. Huh? Huh?

577
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:02,957
I could kill you right now.

578
00:50:02,958 --> 00:50:05,293
But I want my fucking money.

579
00:50:05,877 --> 00:50:07,337
Pay up or die.

580
00:50:10,549 --> 00:50:11,675
Wait!

581
00:50:14,469 --> 00:50:16,178
Get the fuck off me!

582
00:50:28,275 --> 00:50:30,318
Where the fuck are we?

